<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan imposes 10 pct duty on sugar.</title>
<headline>Pakistan imposes 10 pct duty on sugar.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani authorities on Tuesday imposed a 10 percent regulatory duty on sugar imports, saying the action would help the local sugar industry.</p>
<p>&quot;This would enable the sugar industry to offload its stocks in the market and also enable growers to receive payments promptly,&quot; a government statement said.</p>
<p>The action by Economic Coordination Committee of the cabinet follows sugar mills' demand for higher duties on sugar imports.</p>
<p>&quot;In view of the adequate stock position, it was decided to impose a regulatory duty of 10 percent on sugar imports with immediate effect,&quot; the government statement said.</p>
</text>
